<code>assert (0 <= setOrder.indexOf(object) && setOrder.indexOf(object) <= \old(this.size())) => this.contains(object);</code>

However, given the context and the comment, it seems more appropriate to express that if the object was successfully added, it should be present in the set. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert \result => this.contains(object);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (0 <= indexOf(object) && indexOf(object) <= \old(this.size())) => this.contains(object);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (0 <= setOrder.indexOf(object) && setOrder.indexOf(object) <= \old(this.size())) => this.contains(object);</code>
--------------------
